Text:
fearlessManager is a program. The 'single' manager receives the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library; only fearlessManager writes projects.info.
The Info of projects.info is a ProjectsInfo.
Errors are produced by notations invalidEdit(ProjectsInfo,Message), notProjectsInfo(Base16), notNamed(Message) and noProjectNamed(Message), left undefined in the design.
Info[..] makes a new Info with a little difference; for example ProjectsInfo[+=Project] makes a new Info where the list contains also that Project.
Message[Target=Target'] makes a new Message where Target is replaced by Target'.
fearlessManager.names is a Names held in memory; fearlessManager.names starts as {}.

Grammar:
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)
Project ::= Infos.map("path", TaggedText, "kind", Kind, "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, ProjectName1 .. TypeNamen, ProjectNamen)
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
ProjectName ::= [a-z_][a-z0-9_]*
TaggedText ::= \
  Base16                                 \
  | "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn \
  | "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn
EscapedChar ::= [0-9A-Za-z +\-*/=<>,.;:()\[\]{}`'"!?@#$%^&_|~\\]
Names ::= (TaggedText1->ProjectName1) .. (TaggedTextn->ProjectNamen)

Well formedness:
in ProjectsInfo: Project1."path" .. Projectn."path" are disjoint
in Project: Project."mains" is Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen) with TypeName1 .. TypeNamen disjoint
in ProjectName: ProjectName ".fearless" is of form ValidSegment
in TaggedText: starts with "Str:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path
in TaggedText: starts with "UStr:" only if the EscapedChars are the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path, and p.isStr is False
in TaggedText: is a Base16 only if no Fearless UStr encodes the path it decodes to

Notation: Base16.taggedText = TaggedText where:
- Base16 and TaggedText encode the same path

Notation: ProjectName.resolve(Names) = Base16 where:
- Names = Names' (Base16.taggedText->ProjectName)
- (_->ProjectName) not in Names'

Notation: Message.enrich(Names) = Message where:
- Message.Targets contains no element of form "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Notation: Message.enrich(Names) = Message["Name(" ProjectName ")"="Full(" ProjectName " " ProjectName.resolve(Names) ")"].enrich(Names) where:
- Message.Targets contains "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Notation: ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) = Project where:
- Project in ProjectsInfo
- Base16 and Project."path" encode the same path

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Register" Base16) = ProjectsInfo where:
- ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) is defined.

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Register" Base16) = ProjectsInfo[+=Infos.map("path", Base16.taggedText, "kind", "idle", "mains", Infos.list(), "mounts", Infos.map(), "attenuators", Infos.map())] where:
- ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16) is undefined.

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit("Forget" "Full(" ProjectName Base16 ")") = ProjectsInfo[-=ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Base16)]

Notation: ProjectsInfo.edit(Message) = ProjectsInfo[Project=Project.edit(Message)] where:
- Project = ProjectsInfo.projectOf(Message.Base16)

Notation: Project.edit("Kind" Target Kind) = Project["kind"=Kind]

Notation: Project.edit("Mount" Target TypeName "Full(" ProjectName Base16 ")") = Project["mounts".TypeName=ProjectName]

Notation: Project.edit("Unmount" Target TypeName) = Project["mounts"/=TypeName]

Notation: Project.edit("Attenuate" Target TypeName TypeName1 .. TypeNamen) = Project["attenuators"+=(TypeName->Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen))]

Notation: Project.edit("SelectMains" Target TypeName1 .. TypeNamen) = Project["mains"=Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)]

Define fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo):
A action fearlessManager replaces projects.info with ProjectsInfo
B action fearlessManager tells the manager GUI, if the manager GUI runs, to read projects.info again

Define fearlessManager$readName(TaggedText):
A if the folder at TaggedText has the name ProjectName, return (TaggedText->ProjectName)
B action return {}

Define fearlessManager$readNames():
A fact ProjectsInfo = Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn)
B action fearlessManager.names= fearlessManager$readName(Project1."path") .. fearlessManager$readName(Projectn."path")

Define fearlessManager$checked("Name(" ProjectName ")"):
A action return "Name(" ProjectName ")"

Define fearlessManager$checked("Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"):
A fact the folder at Base16 has the name ProjectName
B action return "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"

Define fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message):
A fact Message.Targets = Target1 .. Targetn
B action return Message[Target1=fearlessManager$checked(Target1)] .. [Targetn=fearlessManager$checked(Targetn)]

Define fearlessManager$fromNames(Message):
A action return fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message.enrich(fearlessManager.names))

Define fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message):
A if fearlessManager$checkedAll(Message) is undefined, error notNamed(Message)
B try fearlessManager$fromNames(Message)
C action fearlessManager$readNames()
D try fearlessManager$fromNames(Message)
E action error noProjectNamed(Message)

Define fearlessManager$receive(EditMetadata Base16):
A if the file at Base16 holds ProjectsInfo serialized, return fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo)
B action error notProjectsInfo(Base16)

Define fearlessManager$receive(Message):
A fact No other Define of fearlessManager$receive(Message) holds.
B try fearlessManager$write(ProjectsInfo.edit(Message))
C action error invalidEdit(ProjectsInfo,Message)

Story:
A event fearlessManager receives Message from fearlessMessage.
B action fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message))
C after fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message)) ends with no error.
D action fearlessManager answers "Applied\n"

Story:
A event fearlessManager receives Message from fearlessMessage.
B action fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message))
C after fearlessManager$receive(fearlessManager$updateNamesOf(Message)) ends with Error.
D action fearlessManager answers "Refused\n" Error

Implementation notes:
notProjectsInfo(Base16) could be triggered because the file does not exists, or because it exists and is not a valid info, or it is a valid info that is not a valid ProjectsInfo, including all the well formedness. The error should investigate and report detail error informations, in the style of Frontend compile errors.
In the same way, notNamed(Message) investigates and reports each Target "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")" of Message where the folder at Base16 does not have the name ProjectName, and noProjectNamed(Message) reports each Target "Name(" ProjectName ")" of Message where no folder, or more than one folder, of projects.info has the name ProjectName.
